      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. When the child exits with EXIT_FAILURE after execl() fails, waitpid() in the parent returns a status indicating normal exit with non-zero code. isTarChildStatusValid() returns false, so the parent logs \"Failed ({STATUS}) to untar file {PATH}\", reports UnTarFailure, and returns -1. The child\u0027s error log covers the exec failure, and the parent logs and reports the overall untar failure. As verified in testing, there is no abort or core dump.",
